  "query_preview": "..Tuesday through Saturday\nWinds will shift to the north on Tuesday in the wake of the cold \nfront, bringing an end to the oppressive humidity even as daytime \nhighs remain slightly above normal in the 80s. Surface high \npressure will build into the Upper Great Lakes on Tuesday and \npersist through Thursday, yielding an extended stretch of dry, \npleasant weather with seasonable temperatures. The next shortwave \ntrough and associated frontal boundary are scheduled to arrive \nlate Thursday night into Friday, bringing the next widespread \nchance for showers and thunderstorms to north-central and \nnortheast Wisconsin. Near to slightly above normal temperatures\nare forecast for next weekend.",
